From 83744136685b50a2da8e08b1bbd92f04a34a2346 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:33:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: firmware: qcom_scm: 64-bit DMA mask like the vendor
 driver

The vendor qcom_scm_probe() sets dma_set_mask_and_coherent(64). Upstream relies on
the platform-device default (32-bit coherent mask), and with the vendor cmdline
disable_dma32=on there is no ZONE_DMA32, so every dma_alloc_coherent() on the SCM
device fails: phone test 33 "error -12 initializing firmware adsp_dtb.mdt" /
cdsp_dtb.mdt (PAS init_image metadata). With the mask, test 34 boots modem, ADSP,
CDSP and WPSS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 5be132796..a3130b8e2 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -3779,6 +3779,18 @@ static int qcom_scm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	scm->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, scm);
+
+	/*
+	 * AVR: like the vendor qcom_scm_probe(). The platform device default is a 32-bit
+	 * coherent mask, and with disable_dma32=on (vendor cmdline) there is no ZONE_DMA32,
+	 * so every dma_alloc_coherent() on the SCM device (PAS init_image metadata, memory
+	 * assign) fails with -ENOMEM: phone test 33 "error -12 initializing firmware
+	 * adsp_dtb.mdt" / cdsp_dtb.mdt. The SCM/TZ buffers have no 32-bit limit on Alor.
+	 */
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret, "failed to set 64-bit DMA mask\n");
+
 	ret = qcom_scm_find_dload_address(&pdev->dev, &scm->dload_mode_addr);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
-- 
